# Butler MVP (Phase 1 + Phase 2)

MVP is keepable household repair + record. Phase 3 (public knowledge platform, domain OS, CV, 10k factory at scale) is out of scope.

App promise: observe, don’t guess; safety over completing a repair; privacy; explain important asks.

## Architecture (do not reopen)

- Deterministic Core: diagnosis, safety, and ranking come from structured knowledge + evidence — not an LLM as sole authority.
- Knowledge graph / packages own engineering truth. Evidence owns observations. Reasoning interprets only.
- LLM = communication/translation only at runtime.
- No runtime web research. No runtime invention of procedures.
- Knowledge Factory research is authoring-time only, outside the app runtime.

## AR / vision (parked)

- AR and AI-generated part images are disabled (`locationVisualAidsEnabled` stays false unless a real curated raster exists).
- Location help = text LOOK FOR + chips. Optional plain camera flashlight with the same text. No pins/boxes on junk images.
- Do not implement CV, live AR tracking, or “wait for Grok 4.7” vision features.
- Camera never diagnoses.

## Quality

- Prefer a long, correct implementation of the named task over drive-by refactors.
- If already done, report DONE + paths and move on — no reruns.
- Every batch of related work should leave the main dryer path compilable.
- Safety: no gas, no sealed-system/refrigerant DIY, no beginner live electrical procedures.

## Knowledge

- Optimize for discriminators (observations that separate competing failure modes), not raw failure-mode count.
- Popularity ≠ correctness. Candidates ≠ production until human approval in the authoring pipeline.
